---
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro"
import TopLayout from "@layouts/TopLayout.astro"
import BottomLayout from "@layouts/BottomLayout.astro"
import { ABOUT, SOCIALS } from "@consts"
---

<PageLayout title={ABOUT.TITLE} description={ABOUT.DESCRIPTION}>
  <TopLayout>
    <div class="animate flex flex-col-reverse sm:flex-row sm:items-end gap-6">
      <div class="flex-1">
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">Hi, I'm Joel.</h1>
        <p class="font-serif text-xl opacity-80 mt-2">A few conversations with myself, written down.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </TopLayout>
  <BottomLayout>
    <article class="animate prose-post about-article">
      <p>
        I write here mostly for myself. The plain truth is that I want to be sixty
        one day, open these pages, and smile at whoever it was that wrote them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything here began as a question that bothered me. I think a lot, and most
        of that thinking lives in my own notes, a personal knowledge base I keep in
        Obsidian. The pieces that make it onto this site are the few I felt were worth
        opening up to the world, a small drop from a much larger ocean, a handful of
        those conversations with myself that I decided to write down.
      </p>

      <h2>Find me</h2>
      <div class="find-me not-prose">
        {SOCIALS.map((social) => (
          <a
            href={social.HREF}
            target="_blank"
            rel="me noopener"
            aria-label={social.NAME}
            class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-sans text-ink-light/75 dark:text-ink-dark/75 hover:text-crimson dark:hover:text-crimson-dark transition-colors duration-300 ease-in-out"
          >
            <svg class="size-5 fill-current"><use href={`/social.svg#${social.ICON}`} /></svg>
            <span>{social.NAME}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p>
        <a href="/resume">Read my resume →</a>
      </p>

      <aside class="disclaimer not-prose">
        <span class="label">A note on AI.</span> I do use it to help polish what I
        write, and sometimes to help me research. I treat it like an intern at an
        editorial desk: useful for a rough draft or a second pair of eyes, never the
        one who signs off. Every piece here ends up saying exactly what I want it to
        say, and I try to stay aware of the biases it can quietly bring in.
      </aside>
    </article>
  </BottomLayout>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  /* Left-align the body with the "Hi, I'm Sathvik." heading above it: the global
     article rule centres at 38.5rem, which would otherwise indent this column. */
  .about-article {
    margin-inline: 0;
  }
  .find-me {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  /* A small, muted footnote so the AI disclaimer sits quietly under everything. */
  .disclaimer {
    max-width: 38.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    font-family: theme(fontFamily.sans);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .disclaimer .label {
    font-weight: 600;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
</style>
